# $map creates PendingCall thunks that are forced when a key is accessed.
# Complement of laziness/map_dict_lazy_values.llt-eval: proves that while thunks
# are NOT forced at map construction time, they ARE forced when the key is accessed.
[map [fn [let x] [raise "lazy-error"]] [a: 1 b: 2]]
---
%.a
=== error
[E080] lazy-error (defined at stdlib/prelude.llt:2447:28-2447:47)
  --> stdlib/prelude.llt:2447:28-2447:47
   |
  2447 | """]: [fn [let msg@String] [builtin-raise msg]]
       |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in [builtin-raise ...] at stdlib/prelude.llt:2447:28-2447:47
   |
  2447 | """]: [fn [let msg@String] [builtin-raise msg]]
       |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in materialized at 5:1-5:4
  in map at stdlib/prelude.llt:2455:64-2455:82
   |
  2455 | map@[doc: "Apply function to each element"]: [fn [let f@Fn xs] [builtin-map f xs]]
       |                                                                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in map at 3:44-3:45
